      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that feeling dizzy can be very annoying, especially when you're trying to maintain your blood pressure. However, you should never change your dosage or timing of lisinopril without consulting your doctor. Dizziness upon standing up is often called orthostatic hypotension and needs to be discussed with your healthcare provider for proper advice. Please call your doctor's office to let them know about this side effect so they can safely adjust your treatment plan.",
      "source": "target",
